\section{Technical specifications and supporting checks}

\paragraph{Exact supporting records.}
The complete polar weight table is \texttt{branches/branch-3/emmy/transfer-audit/audit.py}, \texttt{WEIGHTS}, with row/column \texttt{ORDER} HD, HA, HP, AR (donor, acceptor, hydrophobe, aromatic). Divide its integer entries by 10000 for dimensionless native scores. The corresponding v2 table is \texttt{branches/branch-3/ada/scripts/v2\_wl.py}, \texttt{W}; \texttt{solve} multiplies entries by 10000 and rounds, then divides the clique sum by 10000. These weights are not binding energies.

All four fixed polar coordinates and atom identities are recorded in \texttt{branches/branch-3/emmy/transfer-audit/polar-correction-results.json}, key \texttt{fixed\_receptor\_features}. In the accompanying \texttt{audit.py}, \texttt{read\_system} reads SYSTEM.pdb; \texttt{align} specifies atom correspondence and alignment. \texttt{receptor\_features} sorts candidates lexicographically by nearest reference ligand-heavy-atom distance, family string, then sorted atom-index list, and retains the first four. \texttt{ligand\_features} sorts by family and atom-index list. These are the exact selection/tie rules, without resolving the unverified residue assignments.

V2's \texttt{load}/\texttt{read\_crd} read each endpoint's SYSTEM.crd; the existing source table and \texttt{PRIMARY}/\texttt{ALT} identify archive edges and states. \texttt{features} uses atom positions or aromatic-ring arithmetic centroids. \texttt{receptor\_points} includes every eligible feature with a constituent atom at most 5~\AA\ from a ligand heavy atom: no nearest-four truncation or distance-ranking tie is involved. \texttt{rings6} specifies aromatic-ring construction; no unique tie-broken optimum witness is claimed. \texttt{solve} defines integer-weight clique scoring and the strict positive edge margin, excluding equality. For polar edges use \texttt{polar\_correction.py:corrected\_big}, not the preceding \texttt{audit.py} graph implementation. The model-specific allowances, reuse and preparation limits below remain; these records establish neither physical calibration nor P's executable conventions.
